@coderabbitai full review

First manual review request for draft head `fd4a798586b9a52cdb475507512c2c44a9e6ed63`. Please review the complete BF16/FP16 admission union and benchmark changes, including the FE version gate, independent actual-query-length contract, retained graph lifetime, runtime-scale/Stats fallback, and timing boundaries. This includes the still-open #9390/#9401 prerequisites and excludes the separate #9431 warm-run optimization. Actual targeted CI 43500846861 was requested once and remains the run to inspect.

The PR remains a draft. Code review and CI do not waive the performance/dependency qualification holds described in the PR or authorize readiness/merge.

Addressed the benchmark ordering finding in `50178aa4a`. Every backend is prepared before sampling; host, completed-eager, replan and graph-replay rounds alternate forward/reverse backend order and record the actual sequence in JSON. Each backend retains its own wrapper/output/workspace/graph. Numerical checks, error diagnostics, the original timing boundaries and poisoned/timed one-ULP replay checks remain.

Three CPU controls cover phase barriers, separate state, failed-arm handling and phase mismatches; scoped hooks pass. All16 prespecified old/new CLI processes pass on exact50178 library source, H10080GB132SM, officialFE1.32.3 and loadedcuDNN9.24.0.43: BF16/FP16, paged/ragged, replan off/on, and FA2/auto/cuDNN in each process. Every new result verifies the order/sample counts and poisoned/timed graph replay. This is benchmark validation, not BlackwellFP16 or serving qualification. The previous32 reproduction examples used the original fixed-order companion; they and the original full-study performance HOLDs are preserved. This correction does not establish a cause for the earlier control slowdown.

